IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-art2-governor-misconduct`
IMPORT `g1-art2-9a-persons`

-- g1-tests-art2-9a-persons.l4: tests of g1-art2-9a-persons.l4 (Article 2(9)(a) with the persons in it). ASSUMED, NOT RULED (decided 2026-10-27).
-- Every expected value is decided from the Law's text (src:102 to 104 of the consolidated text), not from the code.

§ `Part 1 — Interpretation: tests of Article 2(9)(a) with the persons`

§§ `The persons`

-- Persons are told apart by name AND identifier. Two Jo Le Bruns have different identifiers.
`Jo Le Brun` MEANS Person WITH name IS "Jo Le Brun", identifier IS "JLB-1"
`Sam Renouf` MEANS Person WITH name IS "Sam Renouf", identifier IS "SR-1"
`Kit Vibert` MEANS Person WITH name IS "Kit Vibert", identifier IS "KV-1"
`Pat Du Feu` MEANS Person WITH name IS "Pat Du Feu", identifier IS "PDF-1"
`the second Jo Le Brun` MEANS Person WITH name IS "Jo Le Brun", identifier IS "JLB-2"
-- The first Jo Le Brun written out a second time: the same name and the same identifier.
`Jo Le Brun again` MEANS Person WITH name IS "Jo Le Brun", identifier IS "JLB-1"

GIVEN who IS A Person
      whom IS A Person
GIVETH AN `Exercise on behalf of another person`
`the exercise by` who `on behalf of` whom MEANS
    `Exercise on behalf of another person` WITH
        `who exercises it` IS who
        `on whose behalf` IS whom

GIVEN holders IS A LIST OF Person
      exercises IS A LIST OF `Exercise on behalf of another person`
GIVETH A `Constitution as to the general control and management`
`a constitution where` holders `have it in their own right and the exercises are` exercises MEANS
    `Constitution as to the general control and management` WITH
        `who has it in their own right under the constitution` IS holders
        `who exercises it on behalf of whom` IS exercises

-- The Bonne Nuit Arts Club: Sam has the general control and management in Sam's own right; Jo exercises it for Sam; Kit exercises it for Jo; the club also records Sam exercising it on Sam's own behalf.
`the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` MEANS
    `a constitution where` (LIST `Sam Renouf`) `have it in their own right and the exercises are`
        (LIST (`the exercise by` `Jo Le Brun` `on behalf of` `Sam Renouf`), (`the exercise by` `Kit Vibert` `on behalf of` `Jo Le Brun`), (`the exercise by` `Sam Renouf` `on behalf of` `Sam Renouf`))

-- Two persons have it in their own right, and one of them also exercises it for the other.
`a club with two holders` MEANS
    `a constitution where` (LIST `Sam Renouf`, `Pat Du Feu`) `have it in their own right and the exercises are` (LIST (`the exercise by` `Pat Du Feu` `on behalf of` `Sam Renouf`))

-- Sam listed twice among those who have it: still the only person who has it.
`a club that lists Sam twice` MEANS
    `a constitution where` (LIST `Sam Renouf`, `Sam Renouf`) `have it in their own right and the exercises are` EMPTY

-- Nobody has it in their own right; Jo exercises it for Sam.
`a club where nobody has it in their own right` MEANS
    `a constitution where` EMPTY `have it in their own right and the exercises are` (LIST (`the exercise by` `Jo Le Brun` `on behalf of` `Sam Renouf`))

-- Two persons of one name: the first Jo has it in their own right, and the second Jo exercises it for the first.
`a club with two Jos` MEANS
    `a constitution where` (LIST `Jo Le Brun`) `have it in their own right and the exercises are` (LIST (`the exercise by` `the second Jo Le Brun` `on behalf of` `Jo Le Brun`))

-- The first Jo has it in their own right and is recorded as exercising it on the first Jo's own behalf.
`a club where Jo acts for Jo` MEANS
    `a constitution where` (LIST `Jo Le Brun`) `have it in their own right and the exercises are` (LIST (`the exercise by` `Jo Le Brun` `on behalf of` `Jo Le Brun again`))

-- The SECOND Jo has it in their own right, and exercises it "for the first Jo", who does not.
`a club where the other Jo holds it` MEANS
    `a constitution where` (LIST `the second Jo Le Brun`) `have it in their own right and the exercises are` (LIST (`the exercise by` `the second Jo Le Brun` `on behalf of` `Jo Le Brun`))

§§ `Persons are told apart by name and identifier`

#ASSERT NOT (`Jo Le Brun` EQUALS `the second Jo Le Brun`)
#ASSERT `Jo Le Brun` EQUALS `Jo Le Brun again`
#ASSERT NOT (`Jo Le Brun` EQUALS `Sam Renouf`)

§§ `2(9)(a): the three worked examples`

-- 1. Jo exercises it only on behalf of Sam, who has it in Sam's own right: the condition of (a) holds, so Jo is not a governor merely by virtue of that.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Jo Le Brun` `Sam Renouf` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`
-- 2. "Another person": Sam, on Sam's own behalf, is not caught, although the club records it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Sam Renouf` `Sam Renouf` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`
-- 3. Kit exercises it on behalf of Jo, who does not have it in Jo's own right: not caught.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Kit Vibert` `Jo Le Brun` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`

§§ `2(9)(a): more cases`

-- The direction matters: Sam does not exercise it for Jo, and Jo does not hold it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Sam Renouf` `Jo Le Brun` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`
-- Kit is not recorded as exercising it for Sam.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Kit Vibert` `Sam Renouf` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`
-- A person the club does not mention at all.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Pat Du Feu` `Sam Renouf` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`
-- Two persons who have it in their own right: Pat exercises it for Sam, who has it in Sam's own right.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Pat Du Feu` `Sam Renouf` `a club with two holders`
-- Nobody has it in their own right, so there is no "other person who has it".
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Jo Le Brun` `Sam Renouf` `a club where nobody has it in their own right`
-- Same name, different identifier: two persons, so the second Jo exercises it on behalf of ANOTHER person, the first Jo.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `the second Jo Le Brun` `Jo Le Brun` `a club with two Jos`
-- Same name and same identifier: the same person, so not "another person", although the club records the exercise.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Jo Le Brun` `Jo Le Brun again` `a club where Jo acts for Jo`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `Jo Le Brun` `Jo Le Brun` `a club where Jo acts for Jo`
-- The second Jo holds it, the first does not: the second Jo exercising it "for the first Jo" is not on behalf of a person who has it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person exercises the general control and management on behalf of another person who has it in that other person's own right` `the second Jo Le Brun` `Jo Le Brun` `a club where the other Jo holds it`

§§ `The derived relation: each of the four constructors`

-- The person is the only one who has it in their own right.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Sam Renouf` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` EQUALS `holds the general control and management alone`
-- Several persons have it in their own right.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Sam Renouf` `a club with two holders` EQUALS `holds the general control and management as one of a number of governors`
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Pat Du Feu` `a club with two holders` EQUALS `holds the general control and management as one of a number of governors`
-- The person only exercises it on behalf of another who has it in that other's own right.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Jo Le Brun` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` EQUALS `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right`
-- The person has none of it: Kit exercises it for Jo, who does not hold it; and a person the club does not mention.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Kit Vibert` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` EQUALS `holds none of the general control and management`
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Pat Du Feu` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` EQUALS `holds none of the general control and management`

§§ `The derived relation: the edges`

-- "Merely": Sam has it in Sam's own right and is recorded exercising it on Sam's own behalf; Sam is the holder, not an agent.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Sam Renouf` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` EQUALS `holds the general control and management alone`
-- Pat has it in Pat's own right AND exercises it for Sam: not one who merely exercises it for another, so not the third constructor.
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Pat Du Feu` `a club with two holders` EQUALS `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right`)
-- A person listed twice among those who have it is still the only one.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Sam Renouf` `a club that lists Sam twice` EQUALS `holds the general control and management alone`
-- Nobody has it in their own right: Jo exercises it for Sam, who does not hold it, so Jo holds none of it.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Jo Le Brun` `a club where nobody has it in their own right` EQUALS `holds none of the general control and management`
-- Two persons of one name: the first Jo holds it alone; the second Jo exercises it for the first Jo.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Jo Le Brun` `a club with two Jos` EQUALS `holds the general control and management alone`
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `the second Jo Le Brun` `a club with two Jos` EQUALS `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right`
-- The same Jo recorded as exercising it for the same Jo: the holder.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Jo Le Brun` `a club where Jo acts for Jo` EQUALS `holds the general control and management alone`
-- The second Jo holds it; the first Jo, "for whom" the second exercises it, holds none and exercises none.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `the second Jo Le Brun` `a club where the other Jo holds it` EQUALS `holds the general control and management alone`
#ASSERT `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Jo Le Brun` `a club where the other Jo holds it` EQUALS `holds none of the general control and management`

§§ `Agreement with the caller-supplied route`

-- A person's role with every office false and only the relation given: what the existing rules read.
GIVEN relation IS A `Relation to the general control and management`
GIVETH A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
`a person with no office and the relation` relation MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS FALSE
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS FALSE
        `a director of the company` IS FALSE
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS FALSE
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS relation

-- A situation: a person, a constitution, and the relation a caller would supply by hand for it, read off the Law.
DECLARE `Situation under Article 2(9)` HAS
    description IS A STRING
    person IS A Person
    constitution IS A `Constitution as to the general control and management`
    `the relation a caller would supply` IS A `Relation to the general control and management`

GIVEN description IS A STRING
      person IS A Person
      constitution IS A `Constitution as to the general control and management`
      relation IS A `Relation to the general control and management`
GIVETH A `Situation under Article 2(9)`
`the situation` description `of` person `under` constitution `where a caller would supply` relation MEANS
    `Situation under Article 2(9)` WITH
        description IS description
        person IS person
        constitution IS constitution
        `the relation a caller would supply` IS relation

`the situations` MEANS
    LIST (`the situation` "Sam holds it alone" `of` `Sam Renouf` `under` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` `where a caller would supply` `holds the general control and management alone`)
       , (`the situation` "Jo exercises it only for Sam" `of` `Jo Le Brun` `under` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` `where a caller would supply` `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right`)
       , (`the situation` "Kit exercises it for Jo, who does not hold it" `of` `Kit Vibert` `under` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` `where a caller would supply` `holds none of the general control and management`)
       , (`the situation` "Pat is not mentioned" `of` `Pat Du Feu` `under` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club` `where a caller would supply` `holds none of the general control and management`)
       , (`the situation` "Sam is one of two holders" `of` `Sam Renouf` `under` `a club with two holders` `where a caller would supply` `holds the general control and management as one of a number of governors`)
       , (`the situation` "Pat holds it and exercises it for Sam" `of` `Pat Du Feu` `under` `a club with two holders` `where a caller would supply` `holds the general control and management as one of a number of governors`)
       , (`the situation` "Sam is listed twice" `of` `Sam Renouf` `under` `a club that lists Sam twice` `where a caller would supply` `holds the general control and management alone`)
       , (`the situation` "nobody holds it and Jo exercises it for Sam" `of` `Jo Le Brun` `under` `a club where nobody has it in their own right` `where a caller would supply` `holds none of the general control and management`)
       , (`the situation` "the first of two Jos holds it" `of` `Jo Le Brun` `under` `a club with two Jos` `where a caller would supply` `holds the general control and management alone`)
       , (`the situation` "the second of two Jos exercises it for the first" `of` `the second Jo Le Brun` `under` `a club with two Jos` `where a caller would supply` `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right`)
       , (`the situation` "Jo acts for the same Jo" `of` `Jo Le Brun` `under` `a club where Jo acts for Jo` `where a caller would supply` `holds the general control and management alone`)
       , (`the situation` "the second Jo holds it" `of` `the second Jo Le Brun` `under` `a club where the other Jo holds it` `where a caller would supply` `holds the general control and management alone`)
       , (`the situation` "the first Jo, for whom the second Jo exercises it, holds none" `of` `Jo Le Brun` `under` `a club where the other Jo holds it` `where a caller would supply` `holds none of the general control and management`)

-- The three existing rules read the relation of the facts; the derived route and the caller's route give them the same answer, for one situation.
GIVEN situation IS A `Situation under Article 2(9)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the derived route and the caller's route agree for` situation MEANS
        `Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` (situation's person) (situation's constitution) EQUALS situation's `the relation a caller would supply`
    AND `Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` (situation's person) (situation's constitution)))
            EQUALS `Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` (`a person with no office and the relation` (situation's `the relation a caller would supply`))
    AND `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` (situation's person) (situation's constitution)))
            EQUALS `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` (`a person with no office and the relation` (situation's `the relation a caller would supply`))
    AND `Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` (situation's person) (situation's constitution)))
            EQUALS `Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` (`a person with no office and the relation` (situation's `the relation a caller would supply`))

-- One assertion per situation, so a disagreement names the situation.
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 0)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 1)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 2)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 3)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 4)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 5)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 6)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 7)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 8)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 9)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 10)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 11)
#ASSERT `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` (at `the situations` 12)
-- ... and all of them together, with the list's length pinned so a dropped situation cannot go unnoticed.
#ASSERT all `the derived route and the caller's route agree for` `the situations`
#ASSERT count `the situations` EQUALS 13

-- The agreement alone could be vacuous (both routes wrong in the same way), so the answers are also asserted from the Law, for the derived route, one situation of each constructor.
-- (9)(b): "a person is a governor whether that person has that general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors".
-- (9)(a) and (7)(e): the person who only exercises it for another is not one who has it, so is not a governor merely for that.
#ASSERT `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Sam Renouf` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Sam Renouf` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`))
#ASSERT `Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Sam Renouf` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`))
#ASSERT `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Pat Du Feu` `a club with two holders`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Pat Du Feu` `a club with two holders`))
#ASSERT `Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Pat Du Feu` `a club with two holders`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Jo Le Brun` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`))
#ASSERT `Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Jo Le Brun` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Jo Le Brun` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Kit Vibert` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Kit Vibert` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` `Kit Vibert` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`))

§§ `Through the headline Art 2(7), with the derived relation`

-- The headline still takes the relation as the caller's input; here the caller's input is the derived relation. An NPO body corporate falls under (e), "in any other case".
`an NPO body corporate kind` MEANS LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
`no model constitution` MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS FALSE
        `published by the Commissioner` IS `Facts about a publication` WITH
            `made available by the person in some manner` IS FALSE
            `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE
            `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS FALSE
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS FALSE

GIVEN person IS A Person
      constitution IS A `Constitution as to the general control and management`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`governor of the NPO body corporate, with the relation derived for` person `under` constitution MEANS
    `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `an NPO body corporate kind` `no model constitution`
        (`a person with no office and the relation` (`Art 2(9) the relation of the person under the constitution` person constitution))

#ASSERT `governor of the NPO body corporate, with the relation derived for` `Sam Renouf` `under` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`
#ASSERT `governor of the NPO body corporate, with the relation derived for` `Pat Du Feu` `under` `a club with two holders`
-- Jo only exercises it for Sam: not a governor merely by virtue of that (2(9)(a)).
#ASSERT NOT `governor of the NPO body corporate, with the relation derived for` `Jo Le Brun` `under` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`
#ASSERT NOT `governor of the NPO body corporate, with the relation derived for` `Kit Vibert` `under` `the Bonne Nuit Arts Club`
-- Two persons of one name: the first Jo holds it and is a governor; the second Jo only exercises it for the first and is not.
#ASSERT `governor of the NPO body corporate, with the relation derived for` `Jo Le Brun` `under` `a club with two Jos`
#ASSERT NOT `governor of the NPO body corporate, with the relation derived for` `the second Jo Le Brun` `under` `a club with two Jos`
